  "narrative": "All estimates were interpreted as already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so a positive value supports the registered claim and a negative value contradicts it. The new validation evidence resolves several important priorities. H7, MSI-high versus WRN dependency, is now independently supported. The discovery signed contrast was +0.790, 95% CI [0.760,0.819], and the independent validation signed contrast was +0.812 with a stringent interval [0.765,0.858]. The two point estimates are nearly identical, and the validation lower bound is far above zero and far above a practical 10%-scale change for WRN scores. In raw terms, MSI-high lines have markedly more negative WRN dependency scores, indicating stronger WRN dependency. I therefore accept H7 as a scientifically meaningful association in this supplied dataset and close direct follow-up on the main effect. This remains an association, not causal evidence or a generalizable clinical claim.\n\nThe response deadline for H3 requires reassessing the EGFR-amplification main effect. The discovery evidence was borderline and not decisive: signed +0.025, CI [-0.0003,0.0507]. The independent validation is near null: signed +0.0015, CI [-0.043,0.046]. The validation point estimate is far below a clinically meaningful scale for EGFR dependency, and it does not replicate the discovery signal. However, the validation interval still includes both positive values around the 10% threshold and negative values, so this is not a definitive exclusion of a moderate effect. Because the claim was never accepted and the validation does not provide support, I leave H3 unresolved but close further investigation rather than spend more resources on a failed replication candidate. This is not evidence that EGFR amplification is irrelevant in all contexts; it is evidence that this supplied dataset does not support a meaningful accepted association for the registered direction.\n\nH39, RB1 loss versus POLR2A dependency, shows the same pattern after its validation request. Discovery was borderline positive, signed +0.0249, CI [-0.0009,0.0507], but independent validation is essentially centered at zero: signed +0.00019, CI [-0.0384,0.0388]. The validation fails to support the proposed stronger POLR2A dependency under RB1 loss. The interval remains wide enough to include clinically meaningful positive and negative values, so I do not claim a precise null. I therefore leave H39 unresolved but close the main-effect investigation because the validation does not justify acceptance or further targeted follow-up. Related stratum tests such as H56 and H47 remain low priority for the same reason.\n\nOverall, the strongest dataset associations are now better supported: SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, with ARID1A-intact robustness evidence; MSI-high is associated with stronger WRN dependency, now independently validated; KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, with STK11-intact robustness; and PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency, independently validated and robust in TP53-intact and PIK3CA-intact strata. The next best allocation is to test technical and subtype robustness of the accepted effects, using the registered batch_a claims H58-H61 and the newly registered adenocarcinoma main-effect claims for SMARCA2, NFE2L2, and STAT3. If these remain large and consistent, the accepted associations will be less likely to be driven by the tested technical or subtype stratum, although still not proven causal or broadly generalizable. If any stratum-specific effect diverges, that would justify a narrower association claim rather than a broad one.",
  "research_notes": "Round-3 synthesis update. New validation: H7 accepted/closed; MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency independently supported (discovery +0.790 [0.760,0.819]; validation +0.812 [0.765,0.858]). H3 and H39 unresolved/closed after failed replication: EGFR amplification for EGFR dependency near null validation +0.0015 [-0.043,0.046]; RB1 loss for POLR2A near null validation +0.00019 [-0.038,0.039]. These are not supported accepted associations; intervals remain wide, so not decisive absolute nulls. Current robust accepted dataset associations: H6 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2; H7 MSI-high -> stronger WRN; H13 KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2; H41 PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3; plus robust strata H46/H48 PTEN-STAT3, H49 SMARCA4-SMARCA2 ARID1A-intact, H50 MSI-WRN TP53-intact, H51 KEAP1-NFE2L2 STK11-intact. Next analyze priorities: registered batch_a robustness H58-H61, subtype main effects H14/H15/H62-H64, and if useful PTEN-STAT3 modifier H45; do not prioritize EGFR/RB1 borderline candidates further unless new strong evidence appears. All accepted claims remain associations in supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable."
